[{"sha":"4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDRkNDk1ZTM3OWE5ZWM1OWU3NWZiNzNiYTRiYmVkN2NmZDkwZjkzNTg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358","author":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-06-03T10:25:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-06-03T11:17:38Z"},"tree":{"sha":"1a366135a78673346a93c71c5fefc85ac34f9f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/1a366135a78673346a93c71c5fefc85ac34f9f6e"},"message":"policy: add NodeNeedsPeerRecompute predicate\n\nReports whether a node's online/offline transition forces peers to recompute their netmap. True for subnet routers, relay targets (tailscale.com/cap/relay), and via targets; false otherwise.\n\nThe relay-target IP set and via-target tag set are precompiled from the grants in updateLocked, alongside the existing filter, so the per-node check is a cheap set lookup. Keyed on the node itself, so an ordinary node in a tailnet that uses relay or via for other nodes is still classified as not needing a recompute.\n\nUpdates #3293","parents":[{"sha":"171fd7a3c54156965753a63639cdcafcd50c8d67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/171fd7a3c54156965753a63639cdcafcd50c8d67","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/171fd7a3c54156965753a63639cdcafcd50c8d67"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null},"event":"committed"},{"sha":"274231e0568cb6829943a1e0368b6b5efb6ce0db","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDI3NDIzMWUwNTY4Y2I2ODI5OTQzYTFlMDM2OGI2YjVlZmI2Y2UwZGI","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/274231e0568cb6829943a1e0368b6b5efb6ce0db","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/274231e0568cb6829943a1e0368b6b5efb6ce0db","author":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-06-03T10:25:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-06-03T11:17:38Z"},"tree":{"sha":"7c7e52f513618e603107ba42f5a2388800e19e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/7c7e52f513618e603107ba42f5a2388800e19e75"},"message":"state: gate reconnect PolicyChange on NodeNeedsPeerRecompute\n\nConnect and Disconnect appended change.PolicyChange() on every reconnect. PolicyChange sets RequiresRuntimePeerComputation, so the batcher rebuilt a full netmap (packet filters, SSH policy, peer serialization) for every connected node — O(N) per reconnect, O(N^2) on a restart storm. On a small VM this saturated CPU after the v0.28 -> v0.29 upgrade.\n\nEmit it only when the node's online state changes what peers compute: subnet routers, relay targets, and via targets. An ordinary reconnect now sends just the lightweight online/offline peer patch. Relay and via targets still recompute, so peers drop a stale PeerRelay allocation when a relay goes offline.\n\nFixes #3293","parents":[{"sha":"4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/4d495e379a9ec59e75fb73ba4bbed7cfd90f9358"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null},"event":"committed"},{"id":26284913792,"node_id":"RFRE_lADOEFLz888AAAABEPMA7s8AAAAGHrP0gA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/26284913792","actor":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","foll